15. Expected Results
The project should aim for one of these defensible outcomes.
Best outcome
Selective decomposition improves unsupported-claim F1 by 3–5 points over sentence-level verification and reduces LLM calls by 30–50% compared to full decomposition.
Acceptable outcome
Selective decomposition performs similarly to full decomposition but uses significantly fewer LLM calls.
Still publishable outcome
Selective decomposition does not beat full decomposition, but error analysis shows when decomposition helps and when it hurts. The contribution becomes an empirical study of decomposition strategies for RAG hallucination auditing.
Bad outcome
Selective decomposition is worse than sentence-level verification and does not reduce cost meaningfully. In that case, the project must be reframed as an error analysis paper.
