27. Main Risks and Mitigations
Risk 1: Claim decomposition is poor
Mitigation:
Use simple rule-based decomposition first.
Only call LLM on complex sentences.
Manually inspect 100 examples.
Risk 2: Dataset labels do not map cleanly
Mitigation:
Keep AttributionBench for claim-level verification.
Use RAGTruth mainly for answer-level and span-level evaluation.
Document label mapping clearly.
Risk 3: Verifier performs badly
Mitigation:
Compare multiple verifiers.
Use NLI as baseline.
Use MiniCheck if available.
Use LLM fallback for uncertain cases.
Risk 4: No improvement over full decomposition
Mitigation:
Frame contribution as cost-efficient approximation.
Report performance-cost tradeoff.
Risk 5: Professor says it is just a wrapper around LLMs
Mitigation:
Show controlled experiments.
Show ablation studies.
Show cost comparison.
Show that the contribution is decomposition strategy and evidence-localized auditing, not just prompting.
