28. Final Research Claim
The final paper should make this claim:
This work shows that selectively decomposing complex answer sentences into atomic claims enables practical claim-level hallucination auditing for RAG systems. Compared to sentence-level verification, it improves unsupported-claim localization. Compared to full decomposition, it reduces unnecessary LLM calls while maintaining similar verification quality.
This is the cleanest defensible claim.
